#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Land a PR with the REST squash merge, reacting to GitHub instead of predicting it.

Extensionless and executable because agents type it as a command mid-session,
like push-branch and settle-push.

One call replaces the merge recipe agents carried as prose (issue #151, the
most repeated procedure in this project). The prose was a model of GitHub's
merge behavior; this attempts and reacts, which stays correct when GitHub
moves:

- REST, never the `gh pr merge` porcelain: the porcelain's client-side
  mergeable-state check refuses squashes the API accepts (PR #25), and
  `--auto` on an unsigned-tip branch reports blocked and never fires even
  with every gate green (PR #84). The server creates and signs the squash
  commit itself, so `required_signatures` on `main` is satisfied regardless
  of the branch's own commits.
- HTTP 405 is GitHub saying required gates are unmet, in its own words.
  That is the one outcome where arming auto-merge is correct, so this
  arms it here, through GraphQL `enablePullRequestAutoMerge` with
  `expectedHeadOid` set to the pinned SHA, and exits 2: the caller stops,
  and GitHub lands that head when the gates pass. The porcelain's
  `gh pr merge --auto` pins nothing, and thirteen of fourteen landings on
  2026-10-10 typed it as a second command after this exit (#1026). An
  arming GitHub refuses is answered with one more merge attempt on the
  same pin, because a PR that is already mergeable is one GitHub will not
  arm: the last gate can go green in the seconds between the attempt and
  the arm, and #1413 sat approved for four hours on that race (#1417). The
  retry needs no reading of the refusal's words: a moved head is 409 and
  unmet gates are 405 again, which exits 1 with both messages and nothing
  armed. Under `--wait` the gates were just proven green, so a 405 there
  exits 2 with nothing armed, for a reader.
- HTTP 403 on a PR touching `.github/workflows/**` is the app token's
  standing refusal (issue #136); that merge belongs to the admin PAT, the
  BDFL's alone. With GH_ADMIN_TOKEN present the merge retries on it once;
  absent, the failure names whose merge this is. The retry is the one place
  with pre-checks, because an admin credential can bypass the server-side
  enforcement that makes attempt-and-react safe for the app token: the PR
  must actually touch `.github/workflows/**` (the one 403 the PAT exists
  to absorb; any other 403 is news to read, never to route around, since
  the PAT never lands a routine merge), and every ruleset-required status
  check must be proven green on the pinned SHA. An unreadable ruleset,
  an empty required-check list, or an unreadable file list each refuse
  escalation loudly; a vacuous truth is not proof. The proof covers
  required status checks, the gates this pipeline owns, and does not
  model other rule types.
- The merge pins a head SHA (409 on mismatch), so a push landing between
  the caller's decision and this call fails loud instead of shipping
  unreviewed content. Default pin is the head read here; pass --sha for
  the head the verdict actually covered, in full or as a prefix of at
  least MIN_SHA characters (the twelve merge-pr's own messages print; a
  stalled-prs recipe carries the full oid; a shorter prefix is a pin an
  attacker can forge by hashing, 2^28 for seven).
- The target must match PR_NUMBER when the caller's environment carries
  one (a review session, agent-review.yml's Claude step). Issue #771 was
  a review scoped to #768 that merged #770 instead, a wrong resolution
  reaching this script's argument. PR #772 tried to catch that class at
  the Bash boundary with a regex over the unexpanded command text and
  lost six review rounds to newlines, subshells, pipes and indirected
  variables before either resolving the real bug: the check belongs
  where the number is already a concrete string, not where it is still
  shell syntax an adversarial-shaped matcher can never fully parse.
- A PR touching `.github/workflows/` is the BDFL's to merge (GOVERNANCE
  "Merging", the operator's ruling in #136), and the seat is read from
  ROLE, which every agent workflow exports: any other seat is refused
  before any wait or merge, a shell with no ROLE being a human's. The
  platform 403 that once enforced the rule is gone, and on 2026-10-18
  the reviewer seat landed #1363 on the app token against its own
  verdict, so the rule lives here and not in a prompt line.

- `--wait` is the foreground wait that GOVERNANCE "Merging" and the BDFL
  prompt demanded and no tool performed, so each landing hand-rolled a poll
  and each poll was wrong its own way: a `gh` flag it refuses, the author's
  own comment read as the verdict, a cap reached with the verdict three
  minutes old (issue #842: 37 runner minutes of `sleep`). It polls the
  pinned head until the `review` check run has concluded there, and only
  then reads the verdict, as the typed label pair and nothing else:
  `agent-approved` proceeds to the merge above once every required gate has
  concluded green, `changes-requested` exits 3, and a review that concluded
  without a verdict (failure: the reviewer never ran, the thread says why;
  success with no label: paused) exits 4 with the state seen, as does the
  deadline. A green run proves nothing by itself: a paused guard leaves the
  job green and the labels untouched, and nothing strips `agent-approved`
  on a push, so an approval counts only when its label event postdates the
  review run's start on this head, the test stalled-prs applies before its
  rescue merge, shared through verdict.py (PR #966's review). A red
  required gate exits 2 at once, because waiting on red is the cap this
  replaces. One failed read inside the deadline is retried at the next
  poll, never a death: a 502 at minute twelve of a wait must not send the
  caller back to a hand-rolled poll. The caller's shell timeout must exceed
  `--timeout`, and the exit code is this process's, never a pipe's:
  `merge-pr | tail` reports tail's.
- `--gates-only`, with `--wait`, is the one landing where no verdict can
  come: a PR that edits `.github/workflows/agent-review.yml`, which the
  action refuses to start on (its anti-tamper check, #114), so its
  `review` run fails by design and `--wait` alone exits 4. The caller
  states its discretion with the flag, having read the file list
  (GOVERNANCE "Merging"); the wait then covers the required gates alone,
  and the merge prints that it landed by discretion, naming the file.
  The flag's precondition is checked, never inferred: a PR whose file
  list lacks that file exits 1 before any wait, and an unreadable list
  exits 1 naming it, because the flag on any other PR would be an
  unreviewed merge on a typo. Before the flag, 25 such landings since
  2026-09-01 waited on `gh pr checks --watch` by hand, two commands
  where the reviewed case is one (#975).

What this does NOT do, deliberately: decide. Reading the thread for a
request-changes verdict, the workflow carve-out, and the file-list read
before a discretion merge are the caller's judgment (agents/GOVERNANCE.md
"Merging"). This executes a decision already made; with `--wait` the
decision is "land this head if its review passes", made before the verdict
and executed after it, and with `--gates-only` it is "land this head on
its gates, no review can come", typed by the caller and only checked here.

Every attempt prints what it did and on which credential, so the transcript
shows how the merge landed; silence is never success.

Usage: merge-pr <pr-number> [--sha <reviewed-head>]
                [--wait [--gates-only] [--timeout <seconds>] [--interval <seconds>]]

Exit: 0 merged (or already was), 2 required gates unmet or red (arm auto or
let the BDFL sweep rescue), 3 changes requested on the waited head, 4 waited
and no verdict can come (deadline, review failed or unlabeled), 1 anything
else, carrying GitHub's own message.
"""

import json
import os
import re
import subprocess
import sys
import time

from app_token import prefer_file
from verdict import approved_at, round_started

REPO = os.environ.get("GITHUB_REPOSITORY", "")
# The reviewer's typed verdict (CLAUDE.md "Issue/PR conventions"): exactly
# one of these on the PR, read only after the review run has concluded.
VERDICT_LABELS = ("agent-approved", "changes-requested")
# agent-review.yml's job name, what the rollup and the check-runs API show.
REVIEW_CHECK = "review"
# The one file whose edit makes a review impossible on any push (#114), so
# the one PR `--gates-only` may land.
REVIEW_WORKFLOW = ".github/workflows/agent-review.yml"
# `skipped` and `neutral` satisfy a required check in GitHub's own evaluation
# (see unmet_gates); everything else that has concluded is red.
GREEN = ("success", "skipped", "neutral")
WAIT_TIMEOUT = 900
WAIT_INTERVAL = 30


def die(msg, code=1):
    print(f"merge-pr: {msg}", file=sys.stderr)
    sys.exit(code)


def note(msg):
    print(f"merge-pr: {msg}")


def gh_api(args, token=None, body=None):
    """Run gh api on an explicit credential; the token rides the environment,
    never argv (hard rule 10). With none, the sidecar's newest mint where a
    seat runs one (#1687), read at each call because a --wait outlasts the
    token the session started with; else that token. Returns (proc,
    http_status), status 0 when the call succeeded and -1 when gh failed
    before speaking HTTP."""
    env = dict(os.environ)
    if token:
        env["GH_TOKEN"] = token
    else:
        prefer_file(env)
    proc = subprocess.run(
        ("gh", "api") + tuple(args),
        capture_output=True,
        text=True,
        env=env,
        input=body,
    )
    if proc.returncode == 0:
        return proc, 0
    match = re.search(r"HTTP (\d{3})", proc.stderr)
    return proc, int(match.group(1)) if match else -1


def api_message(proc):
    """GitHub's own words for what went wrong, from the body when it parses."""
    try:
        return json.loads(proc.stdout)["message"]
    except (ValueError, KeyError):
        return proc.stderr.strip()


class ApiError(Exception):
    """A read GitHub refused or that gh could not make; carries GitHub's words.
    Raised, not died on, so the wait loop can retry inside its deadline while
    every other caller dies with the reason."""


def gh_json(args):
    proc, _ = gh_api(args)
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        raise ApiError(api_message(proc))
    return json.loads(proc.stdout)


def required_contexts():
    """The gate names `main` actually enforces, from the ruleset, so this list
    cannot drift from the one the server uses."""
    contexts = [
        check["context"]
        for rule in gh_json((f"repos/{REPO}/rules/branches/main",))
        if rule["type"] == "required_status_checks"
        for check in rule["parameters"]["required_status_checks"]
    ]
    if not contexts:
        die("main's ruleset lists no required status checks; that is ruleset "
            "drift or an API shape change, not proof of green, so no "
            "escalation (PR #287 review)")
    return contexts


def check_runs(sha):
    """Every check run on this SHA, re-runs beside the runs they replaced."""
    payload = gh_json((f"repos/{REPO}/commits/{sha}/check-runs?per_page=100",))
    return payload.get("check_runs", [])


def latest_runs(runs):
    """Newest check run per name. A re-run leaves its predecessor in the
    rollup (PR #377 carried two `review` runs), so the latest start wins: a
    gate's verdict is its newest run's, and so is a review's status. The
    round's START is its first run's (verdict.round_started), read from the
    same list."""
    latest = {}
    for run in runs:
        seen = latest.get(run["name"])
        if seen is None or (run["started_at"] or "") > (seen["started_at"] or ""):
            latest[run["name"]] = run
    return latest


def unmet_gates(latest, contexts):
    """Required contexts not satisfied in `latest`; empty means proven green.
    `skipped` and `neutral` satisfy a required check in GitHub's own
    evaluation, which is how path-filtered gates (`test`/`doc`/`ratio` on a
    no-Rust PR) pass; refusing them would deadlock exactly the workflow-only
    PRs the escalation exists for (PR #287 review, PR #274 precedent)."""
    return [
        name for name in contexts
        if latest.get(name, {}).get("conclusion") not in GREEN
    ]


def red_gates(latest, contexts):
    """Required contexts that concluded and are not green: nothing to wait for."""
    return [
        name for name in contexts
        if latest.get(name, {}).get("conclusion") not in GREEN + (None,)
    ]


def read_pr(pr):
    return gh_json((f"repos/{REPO}/pulls/{pr}",))


def pinned(sha, head):
    """The pin at full length: `head` when `sha` is None or names it by
    prefix, else `sha` as typed. A typed pin is either a prefix (the twelve
    characters merge-pr's own messages print) or a full oid (a stalled-prs
    recipe, the reviewer's `--sha "$HEAD_SHA"`), and the merge body and the
    auto-merge arm carry a full one, so a prefix pin is widened before the
    comparison: `--sha a67fe4b7dc56` on #1573 died as "moved past
    a67fe4b7dc56 to a67fe4b7dc56" (2026-10-24). A pin that is not a prefix
    of the head stays as typed, for the move-or-lag judgement that
    follows."""
    if sha is None or head.startswith(sha):
        return head
    return sha


def read_lags_pin(head, sha):
    """Whether `head`, the PR's current read, is an ancestor of `sha`, the
    pin. GitHub's PR view lags its ref by seconds after a push, so a wait
    pinned to the sha push-branch just returned can read the head from
    before it (#1429): the pin is the newer commit, and one more poll
    catches up. `behind` is a push past the pin and `diverged` a force-push,
    both moves the pin exists to refuse."""
    compare = gh_json((f"repos/{REPO}/compare/{head}...{sha}",))
    return compare.get("status") == "ahead"


def exit_if_landed(pr, info):
    """A merged PR is the one success the wait and the merge share."""
    if info.get("merged"):
        note(f"#{pr} already merged as {info.get('merge_commit_sha')}; nothing to do")
        sys.exit(0)
    if info.get("state") != "open":
        die(f"#{pr} is {info.get('state')}, not open; nothing to merge")


def describe(run):
    if run is None:
        return "not started"
    return run.get("conclusion") or run.get("status") or "unknown"


def wait_for_verdict(pr, sha, timeout, interval, gates_only=False):
    """Block until `sha` carries an approving verdict and every required gate
    is green, then return it; every other outcome exits here with its code.
    `sha` None pins the head of the first read, so the wait owns every read
    and one failed read is a retry wherever it falls. The deadline is checked
    after each poll, so `--timeout 0` polls once. `gates_only` never reads
    the review: the caller proved no verdict can come (main checks the
    precondition), so green gates alone return the head. A read whose head
    the pin descends from is the PR lagging the push the pin came from
    (read_lags_pin), spent one poll on before it dies; a read the pin does
    not descend from is a move, dead at once."""
    deadline = time.monotonic() + timeout
    # True after a poll read a head behind the pin, so the second such read
    # names the lag instead of spending the whole deadline on it.
    lagged = False
    contexts = None
    review = "unread"
    labels = []
    pending = []
    runs = []
    # True after a poll whose label-event read failed, so the deadline names
    # the cause instead of "gates pending none" (#968).
    unread = False
    while True:
        try:
            contexts = contexts or required_contexts()
            info = read_pr(pr)
            exit_if_landed(pr, info)
            head = info["head"]["sha"]
            sha = pinned(sha, head)
            if head != sha and not read_lags_pin(head, sha):
                die(f"head moved past the pinned {sha[:12]} to {head[:12]}; "
                    "re-read the PR before deciding again")
            if head != sha and lagged:
                die(f"the PR still reads {head[:12]}, behind the pinned {sha[:12]}, "
                    "a poll after it first did: the push the pin came from is not "
                    f"on the PR; `gh pr view {pr} --json headRefOid` before pinning again")
            if head != sha:
                note(f"the PR reads {head[:12]}, behind the pinned {sha[:12]}: the "
                     "read lags the push (#1429); re-reading at the next poll")
                lagged = True
                # Nothing to judge this poll, the same state as a failed read.
                info = latest = None
            else:
                runs = check_runs(sha)
                latest = latest_runs(runs)
        except ApiError as err:
            note(f"read failed ({err}); retrying at the next poll")
            info = latest = None
        if info is not None:
            run = latest.get(REVIEW_CHECK)
            review = describe(run)
            labels = sorted(
                label["name"] for label in info.get("labels", [])
                if label["name"] in VERDICT_LABELS
            )
            red = red_gates(latest, contexts)
            pending = unmet_gates(latest, contexts)
            if red:
                die(f"required gates red on {sha[:12]}: {', '.join(red)}; "
                    "fix the head, there is nothing to wait for", 2)
        if info is not None and gates_only:
            if not pending:
                note(f"#{pr}: every required gate green on {sha[:12]}, and no "
                     f"verdict can come on a PR editing {REVIEW_WORKFLOW}; "
                     "landing by discretion (--gates-only)")
                return sha
        elif info is not None and review == "success":
            if labels == ["agent-approved"]:
                if not pending:
                    # Both stamps are GitHub's ISO-8601 UTC strings, so the
                    # string order is the time order (stalled-prs holds the
                    # same comparison). A None label event is an unread
                    # timeline, retried; a None round start, no review run
                    # on the head with a stamp, is final, because polling
                    # cannot grow a stamp a finished run never got, and
                    # `labeled < ""` is False for every stamp, which is the
                    # fail-open #967 closed.
                    labeled = approved_at(pr, REPO)
                    started = round_started(
                        r["started_at"] for r in runs if r["name"] == REVIEW_CHECK)
                    unread = labeled is None
                    if unread:
                        note("the agent-approved label event did not read; "
                             "retrying at the next poll")
                    elif started is None:
                        die(f"the review round on {sha[:12]} concluded with no "
                            "started_at stamp on any of its runs, so agent-approved "
                            "cannot be placed "
                            "before or after it (stalled-prs holds on the same "
                            "test); read the round, then merge without --wait", 4)
                    elif labeled < started:
                        die(f"agent-approved on #{pr} was applied at {labeled}, "
                            f"before this head's review round started at {started}: "
                            "the label survived a push and a paused or empty round "
                            "left it (stalled-prs holds on the same test); read the "
                            "round, then merge without --wait", 4)
                    else:
                        note(f"#{pr} approved at {sha[:12]} ({labeled}, after the "
                             f"review started {started}), every required gate "
                             "green; merging")
                        return sha
            elif labels == ["changes-requested"]:
                die(f"changes requested on #{pr} at {sha[:12]}: read "
                    f"{info['html_url']}, fix every [must], push, wait again", 3)
            else:
                die(f"review concluded on {sha[:12]} with verdict labels "
                    f"{', '.join(labels) or 'none'}: a paused guard or an "
                    "unlabeled verdict, either is for a reader, not a merge", 4)
        elif info is not None and review not in (
                "not started", "queued", "in_progress", "waiting", "requested", "pending"):
            die(f"review {review} on {sha[:12]}: no verdict will come from this "
                "run; the thread says whether the reviewer never ran (#114) or "
                "its run died, and `stalled-prs --rescue` names the recipe", 4)
        if time.monotonic() >= deadline:
            die(f"waited {timeout}s on {(sha or 'an unread head')[:12]}: review {review}, verdict labels "
                f"{', '.join(labels) or 'none'}, gates pending "
                f"{', '.join(pending) or 'none'}"
                + (f"; the agent-approved event never read, `gh api repos/{REPO}"
                   f"/issues/{pr}/timeline` says why" if unread else ""), 4)
        time.sleep(interval)


def changed_files(pr, refusal):
    """The PR's changed paths, or exit 1 with `refusal` when they cannot be
    read: both callers gate a merge on this list, so an unreadable one
    refuses. Single page of 100 files; a longer PR whose file hides beyond
    it biases toward refusing, never toward merging."""
    proc, _ = gh_api((f"repos/{REPO}/pulls/{pr}/files?per_page=100",))
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        die(f"cannot read #{pr}'s file list ({api_message(proc)}); {refusal}")
    return [entry["filename"] for entry in json.loads(proc.stdout)]


def touches_workflows(pr, refusal="refusing to escalate without knowing why the 403 happened"):
    """Whether the PR changes any path under `.github/workflows/`: the one 403
    cause the admin PAT exists to absorb (issues #24, #136), and the
    carve-out main() refuses every seat but the BDFL's on."""
    return any(path.startswith(".github/workflows/") for path in changed_files(pr, refusal))


def edits_review_workflow(pr):
    """Whether the PR changes the reviewer's own workflow file, the one case
    `--gates-only` exists for; the flag on any other PR is refused."""
    return REVIEW_WORKFLOW in changed_files(
        pr, "refusing to wait on the gates alone without proof no review can come")


ARM_MUTATION = (
    "mutation($id: ID!, $oid: GitObjectID!) { enablePullRequestAutoMerge("
    "input: {pullRequestId: $id, mergeMethod: SQUASH, expectedHeadOid: $oid})"
    " { pullRequest { autoMergeRequest { enabledAt } } } }"
)


def arm_auto_merge(pr, sha, node):
    """Arm GitHub's squash auto-merge on `sha` and no other head: the
    mutation's expectedHeadOid refuses a PR whose head moved, the same pin
    the merge attempt carries (409). Returns GitHub's words on refusal,
    None once armed."""
    proc, _ = gh_api((
        "graphql", "-f", f"query={ARM_MUTATION}", "-f", f"id={node}", "-f", f"oid={sha}",
    ))
    if proc.returncode != 0:
        return api_message(proc)
    note(f"auto-merge armed on #{pr} at {sha[:12]}")
    return None


def attempt(pr, sha, token=None):
    body = json.dumps({"merge_method": "squash", "sha": sha})
    return gh_api(
        ("-X", "PUT", f"repos/{REPO}/pulls/{pr}/merge", "--input", "-"),
        token=token,
        body=body,
    )


def landed(pr, sha, proc, credential):
    """Name the squash commit a successful attempt returned."""
    note(f"merged #{pr} at {sha[:12]} as {json.loads(proc.stdout)['sha']} on {credential}")


MIN_SHA = 12

USAGE = ("usage: merge-pr <pr-number> [--sha <reviewed-head>] "
         "[--wait [--gates-only] [--timeout <seconds>] [--interval <seconds>]]")


def seconds(args, flag, default):
    """Pop `flag <n>` from args as a non-negative number of seconds."""
    if flag not in args:
        return default
    at = args.index(flag)
    if at + 1 >= len(args) or not args[at + 1].replace(".", "", 1).isdigit():
        die(USAGE)
    value = float(args[at + 1])
    del args[at:at + 2]
    return value


def main():
    args = sys.argv[1:]
    sha = None
    if "--sha" in args:
        at = args.index("--sha")
        if at + 1 >= len(args):
            die(USAGE)
        sha = args[at + 1].lower()
        if len(sha) < MIN_SHA or sha.strip("0123456789abcdef"):
            die(f"--sha {args[at + 1]!r} is not a pin: the head or a prefix of "
                f"it, {MIN_SHA} or more hex characters, because a shorter "
                "prefix can be forged by a colliding push")
        del args[at:at + 2]
    wait = "--wait" in args
    if wait:
        args.remove("--wait")
    gates_only = "--gates-only" in args
    if gates_only:
        args.remove("--gates-only")
    timeout = seconds(args, "--timeout", WAIT_TIMEOUT)
    interval = seconds(args, "--interval", WAIT_INTERVAL)
    if (gates_only or timeout != WAIT_TIMEOUT or interval != WAIT_INTERVAL) and not wait:
        die(USAGE)
    if len(args) != 1 or not args[0].isdigit():
        die(USAGE)
    pr = args[0]
    if not REPO:
        die("GITHUB_REPOSITORY is not set; run this from an agent session")
    scope = os.environ.get("PR_NUMBER")
    if scope and pr != scope:
        die(f"target #{pr} does not match PR_NUMBER={scope} from the "
            "environment; a review session merges only the PR it was "
            "scoped to (issue #771)")
    seat = os.environ.get("ROLE")
    if seat and seat != "bdfl" and touches_workflows(
            pr, "refusing to merge without knowing whether the carve-out applies"):
        die(f"#{pr} touches .github/workflows/, the BDFL's to merge and not the "
            f"{seat} seat's (agents/GOVERNANCE.md, Merging); post the verdict and stop")

    info = None
    if wait:
        if gates_only and not edits_review_workflow(pr):
            die(f"--gates-only refused: #{pr} does not edit {REVIEW_WORKFLOW}, "
                "so a review can come and --wait reads it; drop the flag")
        sha = wait_for_verdict(pr, sha, timeout, interval, gates_only)
    else:
        try:
            info = read_pr(pr)
        except ApiError as err:
            die(f"reading PR #{pr} failed: {err}")
        exit_if_landed(pr, info)
        sha = pinned(sha, info["head"]["sha"])

    proc, status = attempt(pr, sha)
    if proc.returncode == 0:
        landed(pr, sha, proc, "the session token")
        return
    if status == 405:
        unmet = api_message(proc)
        if info is None:
            die(f"required gates unmet on #{pr} after the wait read them green: "
                f"{unmet}; nothing armed, re-read the PR", 2)
        refused = arm_auto_merge(pr, sha, info["node_id"])
        if not refused:
            die(f"required gates unmet on #{pr}: {unmet}; auto-merge armed on "
                f"{sha[:12]} alone, GitHub lands it when they pass", 2)
        # GitHub arms nothing on a mergeable PR, and the last gate can go
        # green between the attempt and the arm (#1417). Same pin, so a
        # moved head is 409 and nothing lands that was not reviewed.
        note(f"GitHub refused to arm auto-merge on {sha[:12]} ({refused}); "
             "attempting the merge once more, the gates may have gone green")
        proc, status = attempt(pr, sha)
        if proc.returncode == 0:
            landed(pr, sha, proc, "the session token, second attempt")
            return
        if status == 405:
            die(f"required gates unmet on #{pr} ({api_message(proc)}) and GitHub "
                f"refused to arm auto-merge on {sha[:12]}: {refused}; nothing is "
                "armed, the BDFL sweep rescues an approved PR")
    if status == 409:
        die(f"head moved past the pinned {sha[:12]}: {api_message(proc)}; "
            "re-read the PR before deciding again")
    if status != 403:
        die(f"merging #{pr} failed: {api_message(proc)}")

    if not touches_workflows(pr):
        die(f"session token refused #{pr} (403: {api_message(proc)}), but the "
            "PR touches no workflow file, so this 403 is not the known app "
            "refusal; the admin PAT never lands a routine merge (agents/"
            "OPERATIONS.md), read the message instead of routing around it")
    admin = os.environ.get("GH_ADMIN_TOKEN")
    if not admin:
        die(f"session token refused #{pr} (403: {api_message(proc)}); "
            "this merge is the BDFL's, on the admin PAT "
            "(agents/GOVERNANCE.md, Merging)")
    try:
        pending = unmet_gates(latest_runs(check_runs(sha)), required_contexts())
    except ApiError as err:
        die(f"cannot read the gates on {sha[:12]} ({err}); refusing to escalate "
            "without proof they are green")
    if pending:
        die(f"refusing to escalate #{pr}: required gates not green on "
            f"{sha[:12]}: {', '.join(pending)}", 2)
    note(f"session token refused (403); gates proven green on {sha[:12]}, "
         "retrying once on the admin PAT")
    proc, status = attempt(pr, sha, token=admin)
    if proc.returncode == 0:
        landed(pr, sha, proc, "the admin PAT")
        return
    if status == 405:
        die(f"required gates unmet on #{pr}: {api_message(proc)}", 2)
    die(f"admin PAT also refused #{pr}: {api_message(proc)}")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
